    "title": "Texas A&M-Victoria women's soccer begins postseason run vs Our Lady of the Lake - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Max Williams- ,\n7 hours ago Texas A&M-Victoria women's soccer begins postseason run vs Our Lady of the Lake We look ahead to Texas A&M-Victoria women's soccer starting postseason run vs Our Lady of the Lake\nVICTORIA, Texas- The Texas A&M–Victoria women’s soccer team begins its postseason run against Our Lady of the Lake University tomorrow afternoon at 1 p.m.\nThe Jaguars enter the matchup with an 8-4-5 overall record and a 5-3-3 mark in conference play. Leading the way is junior forward Ayloni Garcia, who has scored 14 goals this season to top the team in both goals and points. Garcia, a transfer from UTRGV, has made a big impact in her first season at Victoria.\n“Coming over here, my confidence definitely built up, and I’m glad with the way I’m playing here,” Garcia said.\nGoalkeeper Jamie Noriega will look to continue her strong play in net as the Jaguars aim to pull off the upset against Our Lady of the Lake.\n​COPYRIGHT 2025 BY CROSSROADS TODAY. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. THIS MATERIAL MAY NOT BE PUBLISHED, BROADCAST, REWRITTEN OR REDISTRIBUTED.",
